+Feature: Managing Todos
+  As a user
+  I want to add, complete, and clear todos
+  So that I can track what I need to do
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Rule: Empty state
+
+  Scenario: The main section and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+    Given the app has no todos
+    Then the main section should not be visible
+    And the footer should not be visible
+
+  Rule: Adding a new todo
+
+  Scenario: Creating a todo by pressing Enter
+    Given the input field is focused
+    When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then a new todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And the new-todo input is cleared
+
+  Scenario: Trimming whitespace from a new todo
+    Given the input field is focused
+    When I type "   Write code   " into the new-todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then a new todo "Write code" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Ignoring empty input
+    Given the input field is focused
+    When I press Enter with an empty input
+    Then no new todo is added to the list
+
+  Rule: Completing a todo
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a single todo as completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then "Buy milk" should be marked as completed
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking a completed todo
+    Given the todo list contains a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then "Buy milk" should be marked as active
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete
+
+  Scenario: Toggling all todos as completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    When I click the "Mark all as complete" toggle
+    Then all todos should be marked as completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all checkbox state reflects individual completions
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    And I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    And I mark "Write code" as completed
+    Then the "Mark all as complete" checkbox should be checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all clears when not all todos are completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    And I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the "Mark all as complete" checkbox should not be checked
+
+  Scenario: Clearing the "Mark all as complete" state via "Clear completed"
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    And all todos are marked as completed
+    When I click "Clear completed"
+    Then the "Mark all as complete" checkbox should not be checked
+
+  Rule: Item counter
+
+  Scenario: Displaying the count of active todos
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the todo count should show "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Pluralizing the item counter
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    Then the todo count should show "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows zero items when all are completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the todo count should show "0 items left"
+
+  Rule: Clearing completed todos
+
+  Scenario: Removing completed todos via "Clear completed"
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    And I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    When I click "Clear completed"
+    Then the todo list should contain "Write code"
+    And the todo list should not contain "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Hiding "Clear completed" when no todos are completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    Then the "Clear completed" button should not be visible
+
+  Scenario: Showing "Clear completed" when there are completed todos
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the "Clear completed" button should be visible
