+Feature: Routing and Filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by completion state
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+    And the todo list contains "Buy milk", "Write code", and "Pay bills"
+    And I mark "Write code" as completed
+
+  Rule: Default route
+
+  Scenario: The default route shows all todos
+    Given the app is at the default route
+    Then the todo list should show 3 items
+    And the "All" filter link should have the selected class
+
+  Rule: Active filter
+
+  Scenario: The active route shows only active todos
+    When I navigate to the "#/active" route
+    Then the todo list should show 2 items
+    And the displayed items should be "Buy milk" and "Pay bills"
+    And the "Active" filter link should have the selected class
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo while on the active filter hides it
+    Given I am on the "#/active" route
+    When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the todo list should show 1 item
+    And the displayed items should be "Pay bills"
+
+  Rule: Completed filter
+
+  Scenario: The completed route shows only completed todos
+    When I navigate to the "#/completed" route
+    Then the todo list should show 1 item
+    And the displayed item should be "Write code"
+    And the "Completed" filter link should have the selected class
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking a todo while on the completed filter hides it
+    Given I am on the "#/completed" route
+    When I mark "Write code" as active
+    Then the todo list should show 0 items
+
+  Rule: Filter links
+
+  Scenario: Clicking a filter link changes the active filter
+    Given the app is at the default route
+    When I click the "Active" filter link
+    Then the URL hash should be "#/active"
+    And the "Active" filter link should have the selected class
+
+  Scenario: The active filter persists on reload
+    Given I navigate to the "#/active" route
+    When I reload the app
+    Then the "Active" filter link should have the selected class
+    And the todo list should show only active items
